  "body": "CI on head `0a37008` (the merge of `origin/master`, which touches no file in this packet) failed at the `chuan-bi` job of `gate` without the job ever reaching a runner. No test or step ran, so this says nothing about the code.\n\n- attempt 1: job `122282312828`, `runner_id: 0`\n- attempt 2 (after one `rerun_failed_jobs`): job `122283453882`, `runner_id: 0`, finished 2 seconds after it was created\n\nWhen this happened, three other `gate` runs were still `in_progress` (#992, #993, #994) and the master push run `40530195330` was `pending`. That points to the runner queue rather than this PR. That is an inference; the log can't confirm it, because it doesn't exist (download returns 404).\n\nI've used the one re-run I allow myself. The next push to this branch will start CI again (the codex review fix will come as a push), and I'm still watching the PR. Meanwhile, `thu-hoi` was red on `f7659a2` only because `master` was not an ancestor of the head; the merge into this branch fixes that, and `bien_nhan_v2 --root .` passes locally on `0a37008` (rc=0).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
