  "body": "CI on `934a5b0` and `43b96f0` (master `ef34d88` merged in; it touches no file of this packet) is red. **No job got a runner**: `thu-hoi` (job `122361431082`) and `chuan-bi` (job `122361441689`) both show `runner_id: 0`, no steps, and finished 2–4 s after creation.\n\nThis is not specific to this PR. From about 17:20Z, every `gate` and `thu-hoi` run of other PRs failed the same way in a few seconds: #997 (`40549577824`, `40549571806`) and #998 (`40549750366`, `40549745958`). That looks like a problem with GitHub Actions for the whole repo (quota/billing, or a runner outage), not with the code. There's no log to confirm it (log endpoint 404).\n\nI'm not re-running this time: the same symptom is on other PRs, so a re-run wouldn't add information. Locally on `43b96f0`, `bien_nhan_v2 --root .` gives rc=0 (debt 1/60/0) and c75/c76 pass; on `934a5b0` the full suite was 91/91 cases with 121/121 mutants caught. I'm still watching the PR. Once Actions has runners again, the next push or a re-run will measure the gate again.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
